<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 477)</h2>
<p><b>Optimizing a conformed session works.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b>Fixed: optimizing a session conformed from Resolve did nothing.</b> It asked where to put the media and then silently skipped every shot. Conformed sequences arrive pointing at a frame file rather than a folder, and the optimizer only recognised folders — so a 4K EXR conform looked like it had nothing to optimize.</li>
<li>A shot is now the same shot whether Asobi was handed its folder or one of its frames, so the stand-in, its name and its staleness check all agree. Verified on a 4K conform: 3840×2160 → 1920×1080, frames 1001–1122 kept, 1.6 GB of EXR down to 3.1 MB.</li>
<li>Progress names the shot rather than its first frame file.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
